#X obj 460 2240 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 2216 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 2240 ring \$1;
#X text 82 2278 Not on the Poly-800 \, all edges stay band-limited. \; pw1 \, pw2 (64) pulse width 0-127 = 3-97 % \, 64 = square: every \; foot becomes the AND of itself and a copy shifted by part of \; its period (pulse staircases on the saw net). pwm1 \, pwm2 (0) \; the MG moves the width \, 127 = +-47 % (rate mgr / mgf \, the \; MG delay mgd applies). \; sync (0) 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every 16' period of \; DCO1 \, at the exact sub-sample time. swp2 (0) DCO2 offset \; 0-72 semitones \, swe (0) DEG3 adds up to 0-72 semitones \, swm \; (0) the MG adds +-0-24 semitones. Screaming sync: sync 1 \, \; lev1 low \, lev2 high \, swe 40-72 \, a falling DEG3 (d3 \, su3 0) \, \; res and drv up. The sweeps also work without sync. \; ring (0) 0-127: DCO2 times the 16' of DCO1 (XOR \, the ring \; modulation of square waves). At 127 only sum and difference \; tones remain: with intv \, swp2 or detn for bells and metal., f 64;
#X obj 60 2546 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty FM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
