#X obj 60 2776 osc~ 110;
#X obj 60 2804 s~ \$0-fmin;
#X text 150 2776 external modulator (fms 2);
#X text 82 2838 Linear FM of the counter rate \, through zero (the counter runs \; backwards) above index 1 \, every edge band-limited. \; fm1 \, fm2 (0) depth on DCO1 / DCO2 \, 0-127 = index 0-16 (1 at \; about 32). 0 = off. \; fms (0) chooses the modulator \, it does not switch anything \; on or off: 0 a sine per DCO at fmr x its own 16' frequency \; plus fmhz \, 1 the other DCO of the voice (cross FM: DCO2 into \; DCO1 and DCO1 into DCO2) \, 2 the signal at the right inlet \; (about -1..1: osc~ \, adc~ \, noise~ \, another synth ...). Above \, \; the osc~ goes there \, set its frequency and fms 2. \; fmr (1) 0.125-16: whole ratios stay harmonic \, others (1.41 \, \; 3.5) give bells and metal that follow the key. fmhz (0) \; -1000..1000 Hz added to the sine: a fixed \, inharmonic offset \; with the same beat on every key (fmr 0.125 \, fmhz 200: almost \; a fixed modulator)., f 64;
#X obj 60 3106 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Walsh\ loop 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 460 3164 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 3140 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 3164 wsh1 \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3140 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 3164 wsh2 \$1;
#X floatatom 260 3140 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 260 3164 wmx1 \$1;
#X floatatom 360 3140 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 360 3164 wmx2 \$1;
#X obj 460 3226 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X floatatom 60 3202 6 0 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 60 3226 wsm \$1;
#X floatatom 160 3202 6 -127 127 0 - - -;
#X msg 160 3226 wse \$1;
#X text 82 3264 The four feet are square waves of one counter \, an octave \; apart. Multiplying them (XOR of the counter bits) gives 15 \; Walsh functions: square-like waves that go through 1 to 8 \; cycles per 16' period (sequency) \, with their energy near that \; harmonic. They come from the same counter edges \, so they are \; exactly in tune and band-limited - a wavetable the chip \; already has. The loop orders them by sequency: moving along \; it sweeps the energy from the 16' up to the 8th harmonic and \; back \, through the in-between products \, neighbours fading at \; equal power. \; wsh1 \, wsh2 (0) position 0-127 (0: 16' / 17: 16'x4' / 59: 2' \; / 85: all four / 119: 16'x8' / 127 = 0 again). \; wmx1 \, wmx2 (0) mix from the normal feet (0) to the loop (127). \; wsm (0) the MG moves the position +-wsm steps (127: the whole \; loop \, a sweeping \, vocal sound - try mgr 2-8). wse (0) DEG3 \; moves it by up to wse steps (-127..127) \, e.g. a bright attack \; falling into the 16'. Both act on DCO1 and DCO2 where wmx is \; above 0 \, smoothed by mrph., f 64;
