#X msg 360 3824 vcut \$1;
#X text 82 3862 One 4-pole VCF for the instrument (NJM2069) \, measured on a \; Poly-800 II. cut (99) 0-99 = 66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 13 steps per \; octave \, res (0) 0-15 \, an uncompensated ladder (the bass falls \; as it rises) \, no self-oscillation \, kbd (0) key tracking of \; the highest key: 0 off \, 2 full (1:1 \, C4 nominal) \, 1 half \; (1:2 \, C6 nominal). DEG3 is one \, for all voices: egi (0) EG \; INT 0-15 moves the cutoff up to 7.9 octaves \, pol (2) 2 up \, \; 1 down \, trg (2) 2 multi: every key restarts DEG3 \, 1 single: \; only the first key of a phrase. nois (0) white noise 0-15 \, \; its VCA follows DEG3. env3 (0) DEG3 morph as env1 (see \; Controls) \, -1 = own values a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3 (0-31). \; drv (0) overdrive after the VCF (not on the Poly-800): soft \; clipping \, 0-127 = 0-30 dB more gain with level makeup \, denser \; with res and chords. vcut (0) velocity to the cutoff: at 127 \; a soft key is up to 5 octaves lower \, full velocity plays the \; cut set (one VCF: the last key counts)., f 64;
